## Conclusion

This demonstrates how Pex annotations can be used to test the code robustly, and ensure it behaves as expected. Pex also offers a number of useful tools to observe and inspect the code test and generate useful coverage criteria. The generated contracts and tests would be helpful for developers to understand the behavior of the code and to catch any possible bugs.

In a real-world scenario, the ArrayList class should be improved to handle exceptions and edge cases more gracefully. Pex is a useful tool for identifying potential problems, but additional test-cases should be written to confirm correct behavior.

